 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "A missile hit Riyadh's airport. Twelve are dead. Will Saudi Arabia hit back?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "On Saturday, Saudi authorities said a Houthi missile struck King Khalid International Airport in Riyadh. At least twelve people were killed and more than three hundred wounded, they say. The dead include Saudis, Bangladeshis and one American."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "On Sunday, the terminal was hit again. Saudi aviation authorities say a Pakistani resident died and eleven were injured. The Houthis claim the attacks. They say it answers a Saudi air campaign, with more than one hundred twenty strikes in a day. That figure is their claim."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "The Saudi-led coalition calls it a war crime. Riyadh vows a firm response. The U.N. envoy calls it a grave escalation. The airport has been closed since Saturday. Reports say the attack also complicates efforts to end the U.S.-Iran war."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will Saudi Arabia and the Houthis agree to a truce this month? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
